CON-10: let lateral withdrawals take pollutant mass at the node's concentration

The quality loaders already mix each positive source's mass with that
source's own water, but a parity block in assembleExternalLoads() replaced the
lateral share of the mixing volume with legacy's net lateral flow whenever a
negative lateral component arrived, so a withdrawal raised the node
concentration (200 mg/L for 10 cfs at 100 mg/L less 5 cfs). Remove that block
and its accumulator, and book the mass leaving with every withdrawal
(QualitySolver::lateralWithdrawal) at the node's concentration instead of
only a net negative lateral flow.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-10_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
